  "liner": {
   "body_md": "Mountain Goats performed a concise twenty-nine minute set at Amoeba Records in San Francisco on May 31, 2015 [1][2]. This specific performance is the 208th show for the band in the archive's collection [2]. The recording, captured by martins, is the only available audio for this date [1]. The setlist features a mix of standard tracks and rare performances, including Alpha Rats Nest, Animal Mask, Maybe Sprout Wings, and Elijah [1]. Several songs were notable for their scarcity; Attention All Pickpockets was a bustout, appearing for the first time in forty-three archived shows, while Alpha in Tauris and Absolute Lithops Effect were also rare, with eleven and nine archived performances respectively [1][2]. Old College Try and Against Pollution were also bustouts, with the latter being the first in fifty-eight archived shows [1][2]. The Ballad of Bull Ramos was particularly rare, with only four archived performances [1][2]. The band provided spoken introductions and stories specifically about the song Animal Mask [1]. This show followed a May 29, 2015 performance at Showbox at the Market in Seattle [2]. The recording offers a complete view of the night's lineup, from the opening Alpha Rats Nest to the closing Against Pollution [1].",
